      "content": "Forgive me for the detour. To continue, a well-designed ventilation monitoring system should include features such as:\n\n1. A gas detection system that monitors for the presence of flammable vapors, such as hydrogen sulfide, methane, or solvents.\n2. A control system that can adjust airflow rates and ventilation openings in real-time to maintain a safe concentration of flammable gases.\n3. A data logging system that records ventilation performance, gas concentrations, and other relevant parameters for future analysis and optimization.\n\nIt's also essential to consider the following factors when designing a ventilation system for high-density racking systems:\n\n* The storage area's layout and configuration, including the location of ventilation openings and the distribution of flammable liquids.\n* The type and quantity of flammable liquids being stored, as well as their specific ignition temperatures and flash points.\n* The temperature and humidity conditions in the storage area, which can affect the volatility and flammability of the stored liquids.\n\nBy carefully considering these factors and incorporating a robust ventilation monitoring system, you can minimize the risk of thermal runaway and ensure a safe and efficient storage operation.",
